{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "A route deviation is established on this trip's own trace. The governing measurement is gps_trace.trace_distance_km of 17.57 km on EV-GPS-00107, not the rounded 17.60 km convenience copy on the trip record: POL-RD-01 says the trace figure governs where the two disagree, and the trip-record figure may not be cited for the threshold test. Measured against the platform's booked optimal of 14.0 km on EV-TRIP-00107, the excess is 3.57 km, which is 25.5% of optimal. Both POL-RD-01 gates — more than 20% of optimal and more than 0.8 km absolute — are passed, so the deviation is ESTABLISHED. I disclose that EV-GPS-00107 is schema-IMPAIRED at weight 0.30 with the issue codes GPS_DRIFT and IMPLAUSIBLE_SPEED (a single 331.8 m multipath outlier on the final Raffles Place approach, and the impossible speeds that outlier necessarily implies). That impairment is a discount on weight, not a finding against the deviation, and the next claim explains why it does not stop the finding.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00107", "EV-TRIP-00107"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 0.3
    },
    {
      "text": "The trace is not impaired for policy purposes under POL-RD-07. Its maximum gap between consecutive fixes is 0.0 s, against the 90 s limb (a); its largest straight-line jump is 331.8 m, under the 500 m limb (b); and its sampling interval is a steady 10 s, under the 30 s limb (c). No limb fires, so the deviation may be established on the trace itself and no POL-RD-07(ii) independent corroboration is required. The pre-pass down-weight to 0.30 is therefore entry into POL-GEN-02(2)'s confidence arithmetic only. The route shape is in any event corroborated off the trace: the chat log on EV-CHAT-00107 records the rider putting the Whitley exit to the driver, who answers about traffic and never denies the route.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00107", "EV-CHAT-00107"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07", "POL-GEN-02"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.3
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's explanation — that the CTE into town was jammed near Chin Swee and the Newton and Kim Seng route was faster — is an uncited traffic assertion and carries no weight. No traffic_advisory covers this trip: EV-ADVIS-00107-01 sits in the bundle as MISSING with a weight_multiplier of 0.0, and the driver names no advisory identifier anywhere in his counterparty statement. Under POL-RD-08 a general assertion that traffic was bad, unsupported by a traffic_advisory ID, does not discharge the driver's burden once the rider has shown an excess over the POL-RD-01 threshold; the rider has done so. The assertion is discarded and the excess stands at the measured 3.57 km.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00107-01", "EV-CHAT-00107"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08", "POL-RD-13"]
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-RD-03 exonerates nothing here, and it is important to be precise about which way this cuts. Exoneration requires an advisory record that names a road or segment the optimal route traverses, carries a validity window overlapping the time the trace shows the vehicle would have reached that segment, and is matched by a route that leaves the optimal corridor before the affected segment and rejoins it after. There is no advisory on file — EV-ADVIS-00107-01 is MISSING with weight 0.0 — so no adjusted optimal distance is computed, the excess remains the full 3.57 km, and POL-RD-02 runs against the booked 14.0 km optimal. Further, because the driver cites no advisory identifier, POL-RD-13(1) applies squarely: an assertion that cites no artifact cannot be invoked against one, so the absent advisory is a gap in the bundle and not a POL-RD-10(5) escalation trigger. The rider's refund is arithmetic, not a case held for a human.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00107-01", "EV-TRIP-00107"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03", "POL-RD-13"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The detour was not rider-requested. POL-RD-04 exonerates only an instruction that comes from the rider, is timestamped before the vehicle leaves the optimal corridor or within three minutes of it, and identifies a place or road specifically enough to act on, with chat_message.waypoint_hint supplying the coordinate. The only rider message on EV-CHAT-00107 is a question — why the driver exited at Whitley, when the CTE goes straight down — sent at 21:26, after the corridor was already left. It requests no detour, its waypoint_hint is null, and the driver's reply is a traffic assertion, not a rider instruction. POL-RD-04 is unavailable and no distance is excluded from the excess.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00107"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04"]
    },
    {
      "text": "No other exculpatory route is open on this record. The trip record shows both pickup_amended_at and dropoff_amended_at as null, so POL-RD-05 has no amended optimal to re-run POL-RD-01 against; the vehicle is RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL, so POL-RD-12's matched-itinerary baseline does not obtain; and the fare ledger shows fare_model METERED with a null quoted_fare_sgd, so POL-RD-11 does not displace the distance-and-time arithmetic. What is left is a metered, unamended, unpooled trip with an established deviation and no operative exoneration — precisely the case POL-RD-02 is written for.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00107", "EV-FARE-00107"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02", "POL-RD-05", "POL-RD-11", "POL-RD-12"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The refund is arithmetic and it is due to the rider. On EV-FARE-00107 the surge multiplier is 1.35, read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier, which is the only field POL-RD-02 permits it to be read from; the surge applies to base fare, distance and time. So recomputed_fare = (3.80 + 0.75 × 14.0 + 0.28 × 24.0) × 1.35 + 0.80 platform fee = 21.02 × 1.35 + 0.80 = 28.377 + 0.80 = 29.177 SGD. The rider was charged 36.60 SGD (EV-FARE-00107, payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.0). Refund = 36.60 − 29.177 = 7.423 SGD, rounded up to 7.45 SGD payable on the single rounding step the policy allows. That is 20.3% of the charged total: above the 0.50 SGD de minimis, so not NO_ACTION, and far below the 90% full-refund share, so the outcome is PARTIAL_REFUND of 7.45 SGD. There are no ERP lines, no airport surcharge, no promo discount and no waiting-time fee to adjust; the rider's $12.00 estimate is simply more than the policy arithmetic yields, and the arithmetic governs.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00107", "EV-TRIP-00107"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.refund",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The additional corroboration POL-RD-08 demands of a high-volume claimant is present here, and it is present off the trace. The rider's counters are deviation_claims_60d = 5 with deviation_claims_60d_substantiated = 1, which for an excess under 30% — this one is 25.5% — requires corroboration beyond the gps_trace. It exists: the driver's own counterparty statement admits the route driven, through Novena, Newton and Kim Seng Road, a corridor the booked optimal (CTE southbound throughout) does not use; EV-CHAT-00107 records the rider putting the Whitley exit to the driver and the driver answering only about traffic, never denying the route; and EV-FARE-00107 bills 17.60 km of distance against a 14.0 km optimal, an excess confirmed on the billing side as well as the trace. POL-RD-08 forbids this factor being used to deny a claim that is otherwise proven, and this claim is proven.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00107", "EV-FARE-00107", "EV-TRIP-00107"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The deciding fact here is carried by more than one artifact, so the schema impairment of the trace does not force the ruling below the confidence floor. POL-GEN-02(2) caps confidence at the minimum weight among the artifacts carrying the deciding fact, but where two or more independent artifacts carry it the cap is the maximum of their weights. The fact that this vehicle left the optimal CTE corridor and rejoined it is carried by the trace at 0.30 and independently by the chat log at 1.0 and the fare ledger at 1.0 — the driver's non-denial when challenged, and the 17.60 km billed against a 14.0 km optimal. The cap is therefore 1.0, not 0.30, and this is a case to be ruled and paid, not escalated. That matters to the rider: escalation is terminal and holds the disputed amount, whereas a ruling under POL-RD-02 returns 7.45 SGD to a rider who has been charged 36.60 SGD and refunded nothing.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00107", "EV-CHAT-00107", "EV-FARE-00107"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-02", "POL-RD-02"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The rider contests SGD 12.00, but this category's refund is arithmetic rather than discretionary, and it is smaller than that. The trip is METERED, so POL-RD-02 runs: recomputed_fare = ((3.80 + 0.75 x 14.0 + 0.28 x 24.0) x 1.35) + 0.80 platform fee = 29.177, against a charged_total of 36.60. The refund is therefore 36.60 - 29.177 = 7.423, rounded UP to SGD 7.45 — not SGD 12.00. The surge multiplier of 1.35 is read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier (the only artifact that carries it), and the 14.0 km / 24.0 min optimal figures come from the trip record as stored at booking.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00107", "EV-TRIP-00107"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.recomputed_fare",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "If a deviation is found, it is established but not MATERIAL, and the difference matters. The trace-derived excess is 3.57 km, being 25.5% of the 14.0 km booked optimal — above the 20% / 0.8 km establishment gates but well below the 50% / 8.0 km materiality thresholds in POL-RD-01. A non-material deviation cannot support the POL-RD-06(b) uplift to FULL_REFUND of charged_total, nor the POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral, both of which are conditioned on a MATERIAL deviation. The remedy is capped at the ordinary POL-RD-02 partial.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00107", "EV-TRIP-00107"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01", "POL-RD-06"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_pct",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "There is no repeat-deviation pattern on this driver, so the POL-RD-06 uplift cannot fire on that footing either. The driver_profile shows deviation_flags_90d of 1, which is under the 3-or-more limb, and 1 divided by completed_trips_90d of 619 is 0.0016, far under the 0.05 limb, with completed_trips_90d well above the required 40. POL-RD-06 names only those two fields for this test; the lifetime counter prior_deviation_flags (2) is a near-synonym that may not be substituted for the trailing-90-day figure, and POL-GEN-01 forbids using it to ground any finding. A single flag across 619 completed trips in 90 days is not a pattern.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00107"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No pass-through correction can be added on top of the POL-RD-02 figure. The fare breakdown shows erp_gantries as an empty array, on-optimal-route and off-optimal-route ERP totals of 0.00, tolls_erp of 0.0 and airport_surcharge of 0.0 on a trip that ended at Raffles Place rather than originating at an airport, so there is no phantom gantry, no off-route gantry and no wrongly applied surcharge to refund as a standalone correction under POL-RD-09, and POL-RD-09(1) bars re-adding off-route ERP where a POL-RD-02 refund already comprehends it. Nothing is due on this head.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00107", "EV-TRIP-00107"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "INDEPENDENT OF THE ABOVE, no monetary ruling may issue on this record. The GPS trace is IMPAIRED at the admissibility layer — issue codes GPS_DRIFT and IMPLAUSIBLE_SPEED, weight_multiplier 0.30 — and I disclose that impairment as POL-GEN-02(1) requires. It is true, and I do not dispute, that the trace is clean for POLICY under POL-RD-07: point_count 206 with max_gap_sec 0.0 and coverage_pct 100.0, the outlier jump of 331.8 m is under the 500 m limb, and no interval is sustained above 30 seconds, so a deviation may still be established on it. But the actual-distance figure on which the whole excess turns is, by POL-RD-01, the trace's figure alone — the clause expressly says trip_record.actual_distance_km is a rounded convenience copy of the same measurement and may NOT be cited for the threshold test — so the excess is carried by an artifact at weight 0.30 and by nothing independent of it. Under POL-GEN-02(2) the confidence in any ruling resting on that fact is capped at 0.30, below the platform-wide 0.70 floor, and POL-RD-10(1) then makes ESCALATE mandatory: no monetary outcome issues and the disputed amount is held pending a human reviewer who can weigh the driver's account of a Saturday-night CTE jam against the trace.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00107"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-02", "POL-RD-07", "POL-RD-10", "POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 0.3
    }
  ]
}

