    "confidence": 0.85,
    "explanation": "To both parties. This trip shows a route deviation, and the fare falls to be recomputed under POL-RD-02.\n\nMeasure. The GPS trace EV-GPS-00107 gives the route as 17.57 km against the booked optimal of 14.0 km on EV-TRIP-00107, an excess of 3.57 km, or 25.5%. POL-RD-01 makes the trace figure governing and forbids citing the trip record's rounded 17.60 km copy for the threshold test; both gates (more than 20% of optimal and more than 0.8 km) pass, so the deviation is ESTABLISHED. It is not MATERIAL (25.5% is under 50% and 3.57 km is under 8.0 km), so the ordinary partial refund applies and not the POL-RD-06 uplift.\n\nThe trace is flagged impaired at the admissibility layer: EV-GPS-00107, weight_multiplier 0.30, issue codes GPS_DRIFT and IMPLAUSIBLE_SPEED, from a 331.8 m multipath outlier on the final Raffles Place approach and the impossible speeds that outlier implies. It is NOT impaired for policy under POL-RD-07: the maximum gap between fixes is 0.0 s (limb (a) needs over 90 s), the largest jump is 331.8 m (limb (b) needs over 500 m) and the sampling interval is a steady 10 s (limb (c) needs over 30 s). An artifact can be schema-impaired and policy-clean at once, and this one is; the trace may therefore establish the deviation, and its discount enters only the confidence arithmetic of POL-GEN-02. The finding survives the discount.\n\nThe driver asks that the whole case be escalated on the footing that the excess rests on the 0.30 artifact alone. That is rejected. The departure from the CTE corridor is independently carried by the in-app chat EV-CHAT-00107 at weight 1.0 — a contemporaneous record made from inside the trip, in which at 21:26 the rider put the Whitley exit to the driver and the driver answered only that the CTE was jammed — and by the driver's own account of the Newton and Kim Seng route. Remove the trace and that exchange still shows the vehicle left the booked corridor. Under POL-GEN-02(2), where two or more independent artifacts carry the deciding fact the cap is the MAXIMUM of their weights, so the cap is 1.0, not 0.30. (The trip record's 17.60 km and the fare ledger's 17.60 km do not count separately; both are the same measurement as the trace.) Confidence is 0.85, above the 0.70 floor, so POL-RD-10(1) is not engaged.\n\nThe driver's explanation — a Saturday-night CTE jam near Chin Swee — is an uncited traffic assertion. No advisory covers this trip: EV-ADVIS-00107-01 is MISSING at weight 0.0 and the driver named no identifier. Under POL-RD-08 the assertion does not discharge the driver's burden, and under POL-RD-13(1) the absent advisory is a gap in the bundle, not a POL-RD-10(5) escalation. POL-RD-13(2) governs: on a trace not impaired under POL-RD-07(a)–(c), the deviation stands at the measured figure and POL-RD-02 runs against the booked optimal. No other exoneration is open — no rider-requested detour (the only rider message is a question sent after the corridor was left and its waypoint_hint is null, so POL-RD-04 cannot run), no amendment under POL-RD-05 (both amendment timestamps are null), no upfront quote under POL-RD-11 (fare model METERED, quoted_fare_sgd null) and no pooling under POL-RD-12 (vehicle RYDE_X).\n\nThe refund is arithmetic. From EV-FARE-00107 the surge multiplier is 1.35, read only from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier: recomputed_fare = ((3.80 + 0.75 x 14.0 + 0.28 x 24.0) x 1.35) + 0.80 = 29.177 SGD, against a charged_total of 36.60 SGD. Refund = 36.60 - 29.177 = 7.423 SGD, rounded UP to 7.45 SGD. That is above the 0.50 SGD de minimis and far below the 90% full-refund share, so the outcome is PARTIAL_REFUND of 7.45 SGD. The rider's estimate of 12.00 SGD exceeds what the policy arithmetic yields; the arithmetic governs.\n\nNothing is due on ERP, tolls or surcharges: erp_gantries is empty, all ERP totals are 0.00, and the airport surcharge is 0.0 on a trip that ended at Raffles Place rather than originating at an airport; POL-RD-09(1) would in any event bar adding such lines on top of the POL-RD-02 figure. No driver compensation is due: the fare billed 17.60 km, which is not less than the trace's 17.57 km, so the POL-RD-04 shortfall limb is not met.\n\nNo conduct referral fires. No POL-RD-06 pattern is established: deviation_flags_90d is 1 (under 3) and 1 over 619 completed trips in 90 days is 0.0016 (under 0.05); prior_deviation_flags is a lifetime counter that POL-GEN-01 makes context only. The rider's claim history (deviation_claims_60d 5, substantiated 1) required corroboration beyond the trace for this sub-30% excess, and it is present in the chat log and the driver's admission; that factor could not in any event be used to deny a proven claim.\n\nThe monetary effect, 7.45 SGD, is below the 8.00 SGD execution threshold, so it executes automatically on issue, subject to the appeal route."
